      e: "Simple AD is a directory for Windows workloads and workforce use cases, not a mobile customer identity service.",
      f: "STS does not accept usernames and passwords from application end users; identity pools broker the token exchange for them.",
      g: "User pool groups organize users and can map to IAM roles, but temporary AWS credentials are still issued through an identity pool.",
      h: "AD Connector proxies to an on-premises Active Directory for workforce users; it is not a customer-facing user directory.",
      i: "A user pool is the customer directory for need (1) and also supports MFA and sign-in through social identity providers.",
      j: "An identity pool meets need (2) by assigning authenticated users an IAM role and returning temporary credentials scoped to that role.",
