      d: "S3 website endpoints cannot have a WAF attached; put CloudFront in front of the bucket instead.",
      e: "NLBs operate at layer 4 and do not inspect HTTP, so WAF cannot be associated with them.",
      f: "Gateway Load Balancers pass traffic to third-party appliances at layer 3; WAF works at layer 7 and cannot attach to them.",
      g: "Route 53 answers DNS queries; WAF inspects HTTP requests and cannot be attached to a hosted zone.",
      h: "Transit Gateway routes network traffic between VPCs and on-premises networks; WAF is not associated with it.",
