    correctOptionIds: ["a", "b", "i", "j"],
    answerType: "multi",
    explanation: "Every IAM role has exactly one trust policy and zero or more permissions policies. The trust policy (a resource-based policy attached to the role) lists the trusted principals, for example a service like lambda.amazonaws.com, another account, or a federated identity, that may call sts:AssumeRole. The permissions policies (managed or inline identity-based policies) define the actions and resources the role is allowed to use once assumed.",
