    id: "sec192",
    domain: "security-and-compliance",
    text: "EC2 instances in a private subnet reach Amazon S3 through a gateway VPC endpoint. The security team wants to ensure that (1) through that endpoint, instances can access only the company's own buckets, and (2) the company's sensitive bucket can be accessed only through that endpoint, never from the internet. Which TWO controls each enforce one of these requirements? (Select TWO.)",
    options: [
      { id: "a", text: "Attach a VPC endpoint policy that allows access only to the company's bucket ARNs" },
      { id: "b", text: "Add a bucket policy that denies requests unless the aws:SourceVpce condition matches the endpoint ID" },
      { id: "c", text: "Enable S3 Transfer Acceleration on the sensitive bucket" },
      { id: "d", text: "Replace the gateway endpoint with a NAT gateway" },
      { id: "e", text: "Turn on S3 Versioning for the sensitive bucket" },
      { id: "f", text: "Attach a security group to the gateway endpoint that allows only the company's bucket IP addresses" },
      { id: "g", text: "Enable S3 Block Public Access on the sensitive bucket" },
      { id: "h", text: "Add a network ACL rule that denies all traffic to the S3 prefix list" },
      { id: "i", text: "Use an endpoint policy condition limiting aws:ResourceAccount to the company's accounts" },
      { id: "j", text: "Add a bucket policy that denies requests whose aws:SourceVpc is not the company's VPC" },
    ],
    correctOptionIds: ["a", "b", "i", "j"],
    answerType: "multi",
    explanation: "Gateway endpoints support endpoint policies, which limit what the endpoint can reach, for example to specific bucket ARNs or to buckets owned by the company's accounts through aws:ResourceAccount. On the bucket side, a bucket policy that denies requests unless aws:SourceVpce (or aws:SourceVpc) matches accepts only requests arriving through the approved network path, so credentials leaked outside the VPC cannot read the data.",
    optionRationale: {
      a: "Correct. The endpoint policy controls which S3 resources can be reached through the endpoint.",
      b: "Correct. The bucket policy condition ensures the bucket only accepts requests from the endpoint.",
      c: "Transfer Acceleration is a performance feature for uploads over the public internet.",
      d: "A NAT gateway sends traffic over the public internet and offers no S3-specific access control.",
      e: "Versioning protects against accidental deletion but does not restrict network paths.",
      f: "Gateway endpoints do not support security groups, and S3 buckets do not have fixed IP addresses.",
      g: "Block Public Access prevents anonymous and public access but still allows authenticated requests from the internet, so it does not restrict access to the endpoint.",
      h: "Denying the S3 prefix list in a NACL would block all S3 access from the subnet, including through the endpoint.",
      i: "Conditioning the endpoint policy on the resource owner's account limits the endpoint to buckets the company owns.",
      j: "Requests arriving through the VPC's endpoint carry aws:SourceVpc, so requests from the internet are denied.",
    },
    referenceUrl: "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/privatelink/vpc-endpoints-s3.html",
