    text: "A company uses AWS IAM Identity Center for console access to its accounts. Developers still create long-term IAM user access keys on their laptops to use the AWS CLI. The security team wants developers to use the CLI with the same Identity Center sign-in and receive only short-lived credentials. What should the developers do?",
