    correctOptionIds: ["c", "i"],
    answerType: "single",
    explanation: "The AWS Health Dashboard provides a personalized view of AWS Health events that affect your account: service issues, scheduled changes such as EC2 instance retirements, and account notifications, including security-related events such as AWS_RISK_CREDENTIALS_EXPOSED when AWS finds an access key exposed publicly. Each event is also delivered to Amazon EventBridge, where rules can send SNS notifications, open tickets, or run Lambda functions. The public AWS Health status page, by contrast, shows only general service availability, not account-specific events.",
