    explanation: "A permissions boundary attached to each role, or a service control policy applied to the member account, sets the maximum permissions an identity can have, because effective permissions are the intersection of the identity-based policies and that limit. Boundaries are typically enforced by allowing iam:CreateRole only when the iam:PermissionsBoundary condition names the approved boundary, which lets teams delegate role creation safely.",
