    text: "A company has hundreds of S3 buckets across an AWS account that belongs to its AWS organization and has suffered incidents where developers accidentally attached bucket policies or ACLs that made data publicly readable. The security team wants a single account-wide control that prevents any bucket in the account from being made public, regardless of what bucket policies or ACLs are applied in the future. Which feature should the team use?",
