    correctOptionIds: ["a", "i"],
    answerType: "single",
    explanation: "Control Tower controls come in three types: preventive controls are implemented as Service Control Policies and block disallowed actions across the organizational unit; detective controls are implemented as AWS Config rules and report non-compliant resources in the Control Tower dashboard; proactive controls use CloudFormation hooks to check resources before provisioning. Blocking CloudTrail from being disabled is a classic preventive control, while flagging unversioned buckets is detective.",
