    correctOptionIds: ["a", "i"],
    answerType: "single",
    explanation: "Amazon Cognito identity pools (federated identities) exchange an identity token, or no token in the case of guest access, for temporary AWS credentials from AWS STS. Each identity pool defines an authenticated IAM role and an optional unauthenticated IAM role, so guests and signed-in players automatically receive different, scoped-down permissions without any long-term keys in the application.",
